{"action_intent":"validate_routed_wirelength_after_proxy_gain","anti_conditions":["route_execution_not_authorized","parent_terminal_reference_unavailable"],"condition":"Placement HPWL or FLUTE wirelength improves, but the candidate has not yet been validated through route.","diagnosis":{"cause":"placement_proxy_terminal_gap","required_evidence":["place_hpwl","place_flute_wirelength","route_wirelength","route_dr_total_wirelength","route_dr_total_violation_count","route_la_total_overflow","drc_count","sta_setup_wns","sta_setup_tns","sta_hold_wns","sta_hold_tns"]},"effects":[{"direction":"unchanged","metric":"route_wirelength"}],"evidence":[{"locator":"Sec. 6.2, Fig. 3, PDF p. 8","source_id":"paper.wirelength.chipbench.2025","span":"First, we observe strong correlations among certain intermediate metrics (e.g., HPWL, congestion, and wirelength) and among specific PPA metrics (e.g., TNS and NVP).","span_sha256":"57590c2050d12006d2af386296c1436529b706f2c81f931de2246e223a6341db"},{"locator":"Sec. 4.4, PDF p. 5","source_id":"paper.wirelength.autodmp.2023","span":"Moreover, the estimated PPA post-place might not correlate precisely with the post-route PPA from the EDA tool.","span_sha256":"d1194caa403c696d1bf3ad56e7607a3166d0dd17a3c447bcc1d404a6798287e0"}],"id":"strategy.wirelength.validate_route_after_proxy_gain.v1","review_status":"source_grounded","scope":{"metric_pattern":"place_wirelength_proxy_improves","stages":["place"]},"state_predicates":[{"feature_id":"place_hpwl","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"place_flute_wirelength","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"route_wirelength","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"route_dr_total_wirelength","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"route_dr_total_violation_count","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"route_la_total_overflow","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"drc_count","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"sta_setup_wns","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"sta_setup_tns","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"sta_hold_wns","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"sta_hold_tns","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"placement_proxy_gain_not_terminally_validated","op":"true","rule_ref":"rules.boolean.true.v1","required":true}],"anti_predicates":[{"feature_id":"route_execution_not_authorized","op":"true","rule_ref":"rules.boolean.true.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"parent_terminal_reference_unavailable","op":"true","rule_ref":"rules.boolean.true.v1","required":true}]}
{"action_intent":"use_flute_as_secondary_wirelength_proxy","anti_conditions":["place_flute_wirelength_unavailable","treating_flute_as_routed_wirelength","random_pointset_calibration_only"],"condition":"HPWL alone cannot distinguish candidate topology, or HPWL and FLUTE rank placement candidates differently.","diagnosis":{"cause":"hpwl_topology_blindness","required_evidence":["place_hpwl","place_flute_wirelength","net_pin_geometry"]},"effects":[{"direction":"may_decrease","metric":"route_wirelength"}],"evidence":[{"locator":"Sec. 1, PDF p. 1","source_id":"paper.wirelength.wot_the_l.2018","span":"Because signal nets are routed as Steiner trees, their routed wirelengths are ideally modeled as the costs of respective Rectilinear Steiner Minimum Trees (RSMTs) over pin locations. Since the RSMT problem is NP-hard, placement tools typically minimize the sum over all nets of the bounding box half-perimeter of pin locations – i.e., the half-perimeter wirelength (HPWL) objective [13].","span_sha256":"f3082b22c4be0c4b1b78cef760a30f8c46226415e8a5d98d8f45701d8fd54a40"},{"locator":"Sec. 4.1.1, PDF p. 3","source_id":"paper.wirelength.autodmp.2023","span":"The RSMT is a loose lower bound of a net’s routed wirelength due to routing effects to satisfy complex design rules and meet performance goals.","span_sha256":"6ba86873f3d11afb473bc1e7b9b007431a9de91848ee6fd3086692e36fac9008"},{"locator":"Sec. 1.3, PDF p. 2","source_id":"paper.wirelength.wot_the_l.2018","span":"We empirically characterize a qualitatively significant difference in L-ness between real placed net pins and random pointsets. As seen in Section 3.1, real placed pointsets have significantly higher L-ness than random pointsets.","span_sha256":"e67f75ec28afc4843c40372906217ade88f67262ad7cd5aaad531d54ea0a575f"}],"id":"strategy.wirelength.use_flute_when_hpwl_is_ambiguous.v1","review_status":"source_grounded","scope":{"metric_pattern":"hpwl_flute_disagreement","stages":["place"]},"state_predicates":[{"feature_id":"place_hpwl","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"place_flute_wirelength","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"net_pin_geometry","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"hpwl_and_flute_candidate_rankings_disagree","op":"true","rule_ref":"rules.boolean.true.v1","required":true}],"anti_predicates":[{"feature_id":"place_flute_wirelength_unavailable","op":"true","rule_ref":"rules.boolean.true.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"treating_flute_as_routed_wirelength","op":"true","rule_ref":"rules.boolean.true.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"random_pointset_calibration_only","op":"true","rule_ref":"rules.boolean.true.v1","required":true}]}
{"action_intent":"reduce_excessive_place_spreading","anti_conditions":["negative_delta.sta_setup_wns","negative_delta.sta_setup_tns","negative_delta.sta_hold_wns","negative_delta.sta_hold_tns"],"condition":"Routed congestion and DRC counts are exactly zero, all four timing metrics are non-regressing against a hash-bound terminal reference, routed wirelength has increased, and place padding or routability optimization is configured. This is a trial to reduce configured relief, not evidence that its native consumer was effective.","diagnosis":{"cause":"excessive_place_spreading_after_routability_is_clean","required_evidence":["route_la_total_overflow","route_dr_total_violation_count","drc_count","route_wirelength","delta.route_wirelength","routability_relief_configured","delta.sta_setup_wns","delta.sta_setup_tns","delta.sta_hold_wns","delta.sta_hold_tns"]},"effects":[{"direction":"may_decrease","metric":"route_wirelength"},{"direction":"may_increase","metric":"congestion"}],"evidence":[{"locator":"Sec. I-B, PDF p. 2","source_id":"paper.wirelength.replace.2019","span":"It is well-understood that the standard minimum total HPWL placement objective at some point becomes detrimental to routability.","span_sha256":"887fc03b598a13a3e2e3b7511d5c7b774c8b84adb669c6ed95c964c44e08db3b"},{"locator":"Sec. 2.3, PDF p. 2","source_id":"paper.wirelength.dreamplace3.2020","span":"A low target density represents a less dense placement solution","span_sha256":"dbc47ac1e0e7ca6c31fbf33431411280944359f32e5e35adf84af6db01e5516d"},{"locator":"Sec. 4.4, PDF p. 5","source_id":"paper.wirelength.autodmp.2023","span":"Indeed, we observed that appropriate placement parameters depend on many design elements.","span_sha256":"0a19af38701c4052d9229901447200d655bac3fd47fef485fe0eb90394429940"}],"id":"strategy.wirelength.reduce_excessive_place_spreading.v1","review_status":"source_grounded","scope":{"metric_pattern":"clean_route_with_excess_wirelength","stages":["place"]},"state_predicates":[{"feature_id