{"action_intent":"reject_wirelength_guardrail_regression","anti_conditions":["parent_terminal_reference_unavailable"],"condition":"A place-stage parameter candidate improves HPWL, FLUTE, or routed wirelength but worsens congestion, DRC, or timing against the parent terminal reference.","diagnosis":{"cause":"wirelength_gain_violates_non_regression_constraint","required_evidence":["parent_terminal_reference","route_wirelength","route_dr_total_violation_count","route_la_total_overflow","drc_count","sta_setup_wns","sta_setup_tns","sta_hold_wns","sta_hold_tns"]},"effects":[{"direction":"unchanged","metric":"congestion"},{"direction":"unchanged","metric":"timing"}],"evidence":[{"locator":"Sec. 6.2, Fig. 3, PDF p. 8","source_id":"paper.wirelength.chipbench.2025","span":"Additionally, timing-related metrics (WNS, TNS, and NVP) exhibit weak correlations with other intermediate metrics, suggesting inconsistencies in how existing proxy metrics translate to timing performance optimization.","span_sha256":"77515133e2e5534db5e101d2ba5960c25ba85522765c36db3e1250d9e725bff7"},{"locator":"Sec. I, PDF p. 1","source_id":"paper.wirelength.dreamplace4.2022","span":"Besides, a general focus on the total wirelength will simply ignore those timing-critical paths.","span_sha256":"7e7cdcb4d47141ea8695c0a727207b1adbcd8c62876bc98b4f8ed13db7e21c1c"},{"locator":"Sec. I-B, PDF p. 2","source_id":"paper.wirelength.replace.2019","span":"It is well-understood that the standard minimum total HPWL placement objective at some point becomes detrimental to routability.","span_sha256":"887fc03b598a13a3e2e3b7511d5c7b774c8b84adb669c6ed95c964c44e08db3b"}],"id":"strategy.wirelength.reject_guardrail_regression.v1","review_status":"source_grounded","scope":{"metric_pattern":"wirelength_gain_with_constraint_regression","stages":["place"]},"state_predicates":[{"feature_id":"parent_terminal_reference","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"route_wirelength","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"route_dr_total_violation_count","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"route_la_total_overflow","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"drc_count","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"sta_setup_wns","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"sta_setup_tns","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"sta_hold_wns","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"sta_hold_tns","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"wirelength_gain_with_terminal_guardrail_regression","op":"true","rule_ref":"rules.boolean.true.v1","required":true}],"anti_predicates":[{"feature_id":"parent_terminal_reference_unavailable","op":"true","rule_ref":"rules.boolean.true.v1","required":true}]}
{"action_intent":"reject_post_legalization_rebound","anti_conditions":["parent_terminal_reference_unavailable","downstream_evidence_unavailable"],"condition":"A candidate improves a placement proxy or global-routing result, but legalization or detailed route reverses the gain or loses feasibility.","diagnosis":{"cause":"downstream_legalization_or_route_rebound","required_evidence":["pre_legalization_wirelength","post_legalization_wirelength","route_wirelength","route_dr_total_wirelength","route_dr_total_violation_count"]},"effects":[{"direction":"unchanged","metric":"route_wirelength"}],"evidence":[{"locator":"Sec. 2, PDF p. 2","source_id":"paper.wirelength.ropt.2013","span":"Indeed, a good global routing solution does not imply that a feasible detailed routing solution exists.","span_sha256":"e1c6797d59574cd3d11a9682e07dd28842d6909d1a7260e2d7bc672d5c6ea947"},{"locator":"Sec. 4.1, PDF p. 5","source_id":"paper.wirelength.ropt.2013","span":"This implies that even though the global re-placement may optimize a global routing instance, the legalization stage can worsen the global routing result when the legalizer is oblivious to the global routing instance.","span_sha256":"de012a7fb39217eceda0600a73c46262d40e04034543fddca7022b0ca165f0b5"}],"id":"strategy.wirelength.reject_post_legalization_rebound.v1","review_status":"source_grounded","scope":{"metric_pattern":"post_legalization_or_route_rebound","stages":["place"]},"state_predicates":[{"feature_id":"pre_legalization_wirelength","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"post_legalization_wirelength","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"route_wirelength","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"route_dr_total_wirelength","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"route_dr_total_violation_count","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.