{"action_intent":"reject_macro_hpwl_only_gain","anti_conditions":["full_netlist_hpwl_unavailable","route_metrics_unavailable","timing_metrics_unavailable"],"condition":"MacroHPWL improves while full-netlist HPWL, congestion, routed wirelength, or timing does not improve consistently.","diagnosis":{"cause":"macro_hpwl_overfitting","required_evidence":["macro_hpwl","place_hpwl","route_wirelength","route_dr_total_violation_count","sta_setup_wns","sta_setup_tns","sta_hold_wns","sta_hold_tns"]},"effects":[{"direction":"unchanged","metric":"congestion"},{"direction":"unchanged","metric":"timing"}],"evidence":[{"locator":"Sec. 6.3, Figs. 4-5, PDF p. 9","source_id":"paper.wirelength.chipbench.2025","span":"While this reduces MacroHPWL by shortening macro-to-macro connections, it pushes standard cells to the periphery and introduces severe routing congestion. Macro clusters consume valuable routing layers, dispersing shared-net standard cells and increasing wirelength. These longer and more complex routing paths result in higher path delays, leading to degraded WNS and TNS.","span_sha256":"d8995a8c2572e60f7508c1d03cf3a688f0da7e29f2a3af6f85bf166a717169ee"}],"id":"strategy.wirelength.reject_macro_hpwl_only_gain.v1","review_status":"source_grounded","scope":{"metric_pattern":"macro_hpwl_only_gain","stages":["place"]},"state_predicates":[{"feature_id":"macro_hpwl","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"place_hpwl","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"route_wirelength","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"route_dr_total_violation_count","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"sta_setup_wns","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"sta_setup_tns","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"sta_hold_wns","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"sta_hold_tns","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"macro_hpwl_gain_not_confirmed_by_full_design","op":"true","rule_ref":"rules.boolean.true.v1","required":true}],"anti_predicates":[{"feature_id":"full_netlist_hpwl_unavailable","op":"true","rule_ref":"rules.boolean.true.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"route_metrics_unavailable","op":"true","rule_ref":"rules.boolean.true.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"timing_metrics_unavailable","op":"true","rule_ref":"rules.boolean.true.v1","required":true}]}
{"action_intent":"reduce_wide_core_elongation_trial","anti_conditions":[],"condition":"Source-derived bounded exploratory hypothesis, not paper-validated efficacy. Change one legal parameter at a time; retain terminal routing, timing, DRC and budget guards. The configured core aspect ratio is above one in die-util mode. Explore decreasing floorplan.aspect_ratio at fixed core utilization. The current value above or below one motivates only the trial direction; the action contract does not prevent crossing one or guarantee less elongation. Squaring a fixed-area rectangle reduces its geometric perimeter, not necessarily net wirelength; macro channels and IO geometry may favor elongation.","diagnosis":{"cause":"core_shape_wirelength_tradeoff","required_evidence":["floorplan_die_util_mode","floorplan_aspect_ratio_offset"]},"effects":[{"metric":"route_wirelength","direction":"may_decrease"},{"metric":"congestion","direction":"may_increase"},{"metric":"timing","direction":"may_increase"}],"evidence":[{"source_id":"source.ifp.core_geometry","source_path":"ecc/chipcompiler/thirdparty/ecc-tools/src/operation/iFP/source/module/die_builder/DieBuilder.cpp","start":99,"end":106,"locator":"ecc/chipcompiler/thirdparty/ecc-tools/src/operation/iFP/source/module/die_builder/DieBuilder.cpp:99-106","span":"    int32_t micron_dbu = database.get_micron_dbu();\n    Site& core_site = site_iter->second;\n    double core_area = database.get_cell_area() / config.die_utilization;\n    double core_height_micron = std::sqrt(core_area / config.die_aspect_ratio);\n    double core_width_micron = core_area / core_height_micron;\n    int32_t core_width = FPUTIL.alignUp(static_cast<int32_t>(std::ceil(core_width_micron * micron_dbu)), core_site.get_width());\n    int32_t core_height = FPUTIL.alignUp(static_cast<int32_t>(std::ceil(core_height_micron * micron_dbu)), core_site.get_height());\n    int32_t margin_left = FPUTIL.transMicronToDBU(config.die_margin_left_micron, micron_dbu);\n","span_sha256":"1bfe87220de993009cf46b50eb23b312e1c5d63d6e87e3335511e530d08478b1"}],"id":"strategy.wirelength.trial_wide_core_shape.v1","review_status":"source_derived_hypothesis","scope":{"metric_pattern":"trial_wide_core_shape","stages":["floorplan"]},"state_predicates":[{"feature_id":"floorplan_die_util_mode","op":"true","rule_ref":"rules.boolean.true.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"floorplan_aspect_ratio_offset","op":"positive","rule_ref":"rules.numeric.positive.v1","required":true}],"anti_predicates":[]}
{"action_intent":"reduce_tall_core_elongation_trial","anti_conditions":[],"condition":"Source-derived bounded exploratory hypothesis, not paper-validated efficacy. Change one legal parameter at a time; retain terminal routing, timing, DRC and budget guards. The configured core aspect ratio is below one in die-util mode. Explore increasing floorplan.aspect_ratio at fixed core utilization. The current value above or below one motivates only the trial direction; the action contract does not prevent crossing one or guarantee less elongation. Squaring a fixed-area rectangle reduces its geometric perimeter, not necessarily net wirelength; macro channels and IO geometry may favor elongation.","diagnosis":{"cause":"core_shape_wirelength_tradeoff","required_evidence":["floorplan_die_util_mode","floorplan_aspect_ratio_offset"]},"effects":[{"metric":"route_wirelength","direction":"may_decrease"},{"metric":"congestion","direction":"may_increase"},{"metric":"timing","direction":"may_increase"}],"evidence":[{"source_id":"source.ifp.core_geometry","source_path":"ecc/chipcompiler/thirdparty/ecc-tools/src/operation/iFP/source/module/die_builder/DieBuilder.cpp","start":99,"end":106,"locator":"ecc/chipcompiler/thirdparty/ecc-tools/src/operation/iFP/source/module/die_builder/DieBuilder.cpp:99-106","span":"    int32_t micron_dbu = database.get_micron_dbu();\n    Site& core_site = site_iter->second;\n    double core_area = database.get_cell_area() / config.die_utilization;\n    double core_height_micron = std::sqrt(core_area / config.die_aspect_ratio);\n    double core_width_micron = core_area / core_height_micron;\n    int32_t core_width = FPUTIL.alignUp(static_cast<int32_t>(std::ceil(core_width_micron * micron_dbu)), core_site.get_width());\n    int32_t core_height = FPUTIL.alignUp(static_cast<int32_t>(std::ceil(core_height_micron * micron_dbu)), core_site.get_height());\n    int32_t margin_left = FPUTIL.transMicronToDBU(config.die_margin_left_micron, micron_dbu);\n","span_sha256":"1bfe87220de993009cf46b50eb23b312e1c5d63d6e87e3335511e530d08478b1"}],"id":"strategy.wirelength.trial_tall_core_shape.v1","review_status":"source_derived_hypothesis","scope":{"metric_pattern":"trial_tall_core_shape","stages":["floorplan"]},"state_predicates":[{"feature_id":"floorplan_die_util_mode","op":"true","rule_ref":"rules.boolean.true.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"floorplan_aspect_ratio_offset","op":"negative","rule_ref":"rules.numeric.negative.v1","required":true}],"anti_predicates":[]}
{"action_intent":"decrease_initial_density_penalty_trial","anti_conditions":["negative.delta.sta_setup_wns","negative.delta.sta_setup_tns","negative.delta.sta_hold_wns","negative.delta.sta_hold_tns"],"condition":"Source-derived bounded exploratory hypothesis, not paper-validated efficacy. Change one legal parameter at a time; retain terminal routing, timing, DRC and budget guards. Routed congestion and DRC counts are exactly zero, all four timing metrics are non-regressing, and routed wirelength increased against the terminal reference. Explore a smaller initial density coefficient while keeping target density, overflow threshold and routability mode fixed.","diagnosis":{"cause":"initial_density_wirelength_tradeoff","required_evidence":["route_la_total_overflow","route_dr_total_violation_count","drc_count","delta.route_wirelength","place.density_weight","delta.sta_setup_wns","delta.sta_setup_tns","delta.sta_hold_wns","delta.sta_hold_tns"]},"effects":[{"metric":"route_wirelength","direction":"may_decrease"},{"metric":"congestion","direction":"may_increase"},{"metric":"placement_density_overflow","direction":"may_increase"}],"evidence":[{"source_id":"source.dreamplace.density_weight_initialization","source_path":"ecc/chipcompiler/thirdparty/ecc-dreamplace/dreamplace/PlaceObj.py","start":2104,"end":2116,"locator":"ecc/chipcompiler/thirdparty/ecc-dreamplace/dreamplace/PlaceObj.py:2104-2116","span":"            density = self.op_collections.density_op(self.data_collections.pos[0])\n            # record initial density\n            self.init_density = density.data.clone()\n            density.backward()\n            density_grad_norm = self.data_collections.pos[0].grad.norm(p=1)\n\n            grad_norm_ratio = wirelength_grad_norm / density_grad_norm\n            self.density_weight = torch.tensor(\n                [params.density_weight * grad_norm_ratio],\n                dtype=self.data_collections.pos[0].dtype,\n                device=self.data_collections.pos[0].device,\n            )\n\n","span_sha256":"97ef1499f85eeed8e25b4e361413bd9734c88decf4bb826e2cd40c75ce0079be"}],"id":"strategy.wirelength.trial_weaker_initial_density_penalty.v1","review_status":"source_derived_hypothesis","scope":{"metric_pattern":"trial_weaker_initial_density_penalty","stages":["place"]},"state_predicates":[{"feature_id":"route_la_total_overflow","op":"zero","rule_ref":"rules.numeric.zero.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"route_dr_total_violation_count","op":"zero","rule_ref":"rules.numeric.zero.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"drc_count","op":"zero","rule_ref":"rules.numeric.zero.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"delta.route_wirelength","op":"positive","rule_ref":"rules.numeric.positive.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"place.density_weight","op":"positive","rule_ref":"rules.numeric.positive.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"delta.sta_setup_wns","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"delta.sta_setup_tns","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"delta.sta_hold_wns","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"delta.sta_hold_tns","op":"present","rule_ref":"rules.evidence.present.v1","required":true}],"anti_predicates":[{"feature_id":"delta.sta_setup_wns","op":"negative","rule_ref":"rules.numeric.negative.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"delta.sta_setup_tns","op":"negative","rule_ref":"rules.numeric.negative.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"delta.sta_hold_wns","op":"negative","rule_ref":"rules.numeric.negative.v1","required":true},{"feature_id":"delta.sta_hold_tns","op":"negative","rule_ref":"rules.numeric.negative.v1","required":true}]}
